IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-base`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-offence`

-- ccc7-s185-applications.l4 -- section 185 (application for authorization) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part VI.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against it.
-- What this section means to the person in the seat: what the police and the Crown had to put before the judge before an authorization could be given about them, who had to sign, and when the usual requirement of
-- showing that other investigative methods failed falls away (offences of criminal organizations, terrorism and the like). Facts are plain inputs; the terms of other sections are MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs named for the section.

§ `Section 185 -- Application for authorization`

DECLARE `s 185(1) signatory` IS ONE OF
    `s 185(1) the Attorney General of the province in which the application is made`
    `s 185(1) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`
    `s 185(1) an agent specially designated in writing by the Minister personally`
    `s 185(1) an agent specially designated in writing by the Deputy Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness personally`
    `s 185(1) an agent specially designated in writing by the Attorney General of a province personally`
    `s 185(1) an agent specially designated in writing by the Deputy Attorney General of a province personally`
    `s 185(1) a person who is none of those`

-- 185(1.1): "Notwithstanding paragraph (1)(h), that paragraph does not apply where the application for an authorization is in relation to (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13; (b) an offence committed for the benefit of,
-- at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization; (b.1) an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or (c) a terrorism offence."
-- The offence the application is in relation to is a `s 183 provision of an Act` (the Act, the section, the subsection). "criminal organization" and "terrorism offence" are section 2 terms: MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs.
-- "where ... is in relation to": a failed "where" is JUST FALSE (periods and "where" ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)).
-- src:3852 | Exception for criminal organizations and terrorist groups
-- src:3853 | (1.1) Notwithstanding paragraph (1)(h), that paragraph does not apply where the application for an authorization is in relation to
-- src:3854 | (a) an offence under section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13;
-- src:3855 | (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization;
-- src:3856 | (b.1) an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act; or
-- src:3857 | (c) a terrorism offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 185(1.1) (src:3852-3857)
GIVEN `the offence the application is in relation to` IS A `s 183 provision of an Act`
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(1.1) paragraph (1)(h) does not apply to the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that paragraph does not apply where the application for an authorization is in relation to"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a criminal organization, or the offence a terrorism offence, is for another section and is not covered
    WHERE
        `the section` MEANS `the offence the application is in relation to`'s `section`
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            (`the offence the application is in relation to`'s `statute` EQUALS `s 183 the Criminal Code`)
            AND (`the section` EQUALS 52 OR `the section` EQUALS 52.1 OR `the section` EQUALS 52.2 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.11 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.111 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.12 OR `the section` EQUALS 467.13)
        `limb (b.1)` MEANS
            (`the offence the application is in relation to`'s `statute` EQUALS `s 183 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`)
            AND (`the offence the application is in relation to`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            AND (`the section` EQUALS 20 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.1 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.2 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.3 OR `the section` EQUALS 20.4)
        `the limbs` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued any of`
                (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `limb (a)`
                    , `s 183 three-valued all of` (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group`, `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization`)
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `limb (b.1)`
                    , `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`)

-- 185(1): "An application for an authorization to be given under section 186 shall be made ex parte and in writing to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 and shall be signed by the Attorney General of
-- the province in which the application is made or the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness or an agent specially designated in writing for the purposes of this section by (a) the Minister personally or the Deputy Minister ... personally,
-- if the offence under investigation is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada, or (b) the Attorney General of a province
-- personally or the Deputy Attorney General of a province personally, in any other case, and shall be accompanied by an affidavit ... deposing to the following matters: (c) ... (h)".
-- The function says whether the application meets the subsection: JUST TRUE if every requirement is met; JUST FALSE if one is not ("shall"); (h) is not required where subsection (1.1) says paragraph (1)(h) does not apply.
-- src:3841 | Application for authorization
-- src:3842 | 185 (1) An application for an authorization to be given under section 186 shall be made ex parte and in writing to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 and shall be signed by the Attorney General of the province in which the application is made or the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness or an agent specially designated in writing for the purposes of this section by
-- src:3843 | (a) the Minister personally or the Deputy Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness personally, if the offence under investigation is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada, or
-- src:3844 | (b) the Attorney General of a province personally or the Deputy Attorney General of a province personally, in any other case,
-- src:3845 | and shall be accompanied by an affidavit, which may be sworn on the information and belief of a peace officer or public officer deposing to the following matters:
-- src:3846 | (c) the facts relied on to justify the belief that an authorization should be given together with particulars of the offence,
-- src:3847 | (d) the type of private communication proposed to be intercepted,
-- src:3848 | (e) the names, addresses and occupations, if known, of all persons, the interception of whose private communications there are reasonable grounds to believe may assist the investigation of the offence, a general description of the nature and location of the place, if known, at which private communications are proposed to be intercepted and a general description of the manner of interception proposed to be used,
-- src:3849 | (f) the number of instances, if any, on which an application has been made under this section in relation to the offence and a person named in the affidavit pursuant to paragraph (e) and on which the application was withdrawn or no authorization was given, the date on which each application was made and the name of the judge to whom each application was made,
-- src:3850 | (g) the period for which the authorization is requested, and
-- src:3851 | (h) whether other investigative procedures have been tried and have failed or why it appears they are unlikely to succeed or that the urgency of the matter is such that it would be impractical to carry out the investigation of the offence using only other investigative procedures.
@ref Criminal Code s 185(1) (src:3841-3851)
GIVEN `the application was made ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application was made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application was made to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` IS A BOOLEAN
      signatory IS A `s 185(1) signatory`
      `the offence under investigation is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the facts relied on to justify the belief that an authorization should be given together with particulars of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the type of private communication proposed to be intercepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the names, addresses and occupations, if known, of all persons whose communications may assist the investigation, a general description of the place and of the manner of interception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the number of instances, if any, on which an application was made in relation to the offence and a named person and was withdrawn or no authorization was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the period for which the authorization is requested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes whether other investigative procedures have been tried and have failed, or why it appears they are unlikely to succeed, or that the urgency of the matter is such that it would be impractical to carry out the investigation using only other investigative procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 185(1.1) paragraph (1)(h) does not apply to the application` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(1) the application meets the requirements of the subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirements` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the requirements` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be made ex parte and in writing to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 and shall be signed by"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (1)(h) is dispensed with by subsection (1.1) is not covered
    WHERE
        `the signature is in order` MEANS
            CONSIDER signatory
            WHEN `s 185(1) the Attorney General of the province in which the application is made` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 185(1) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 185(1) an agent specially designated in writing by the Minister personally` THEN `the offence under investigation is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada`
            WHEN `s 185(1) an agent specially designated in writing by the Deputy Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness personally` THEN `the offence under investigation is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada`
            WHEN `s 185(1) an agent specially designated in writing by the Attorney General of a province personally` THEN NOT `the offence under investigation is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada`
            WHEN `s 185(1) an agent specially designated in writing by the Deputy Attorney General of a province personally` THEN NOT `the offence under investigation is one in respect of which proceedings, if any, may be instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada`
            WHEN `s 185(1) a person who is none of those` THEN FALSE
        `paragraph (h) matter` MEANS
            IF `s 185(1.1) paragraph (1)(h) does not apply to the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE IF `the affidavit deposes whether other investigative procedures have been tried and have failed, or why it appears they are unlikely to succeed, or that the urgency of the matter is such that it would be impractical to carry out the investigation using only other investigative procedures`
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE IF `s 185(1.1) paragraph (1)(h) does not apply to the application` EQUALS NOTHING
                      THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (1)(h) is dispensed with by subsection (1.1) is for that subsection and is not covered
                      ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whether other investigative procedures have been tried and have failed or why it appears they are unlikely to succeed"
        `the requirements` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued all of`
                (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the application was made ex parte`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the application was made in writing`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the application was made to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the signature is in order`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` (`the application is accompanied by an affidavit` AND `the affidavit deposes to the facts relied on to justify the belief that an authorization should be given together with particulars of the offence` AND `the affidavit deposes to the type of private communication proposed to be intercepted` AND `the affidavit deposes to the names, addresses and occupations, if known, of all persons whose communications may assist the investigation, a general description of the place and of the manner of interception` AND `the affidavit deposes to the number of instances, if any, on which an application was made in relation to the offence and a named person and was withdrawn or no authorization was given` AND `the affidavit deposes to the period for which the authorization is requested`)
                    , `paragraph (h) matter`)

-- A period of three years or less, as a Length of time (years, months, days). Used by 185(2) and (3), 196(3) and (5), 196.1(3) and (5), each of which says "not exceeding three years". 36 months is within the limit; 36 months and one day is not.
GIVEN period IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 185(2) the period does not exceed three years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (period's years TIMES 12) PLUS period's months LESS THAN 36 THEN TRUE
        IF ((period's years TIMES 12) PLUS period's months EQUALS 36) AND (period's days EQUALS 0) THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 185(2): "An application for an authorization may be accompanied by an application, personally signed by the Attorney General of the province in which the application for the authorization is made or the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness
-- if the application for the authorization is made by him or on his behalf, to substitute for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1) such longer period not exceeding three years as is set out in the application."
-- A grant ("may be accompanied"): outside its own limits (the signature, "longer", "not exceeding three years") it is NOT COVERED.
-- src:3858 | Extension of period for notification
-- src:3859 | (2) An application for an authorization may be accompanied by an application, personally signed by the Attorney General of the province in which the application for the authorization is made or the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness if the application for the authorization is made by him or on his behalf, to substitute for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1) such longer period not exceeding three years as is set out in the application.
@ref Criminal Code s 185(2) (src:3858-3859)
GIVEN `the accompanying application is personally signed by the Attorney General of the province in which the application for the authorization is made or by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it asks for a period longer than the period mentioned in subsection 196(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longer period it sets out` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(2) the application for an authorization may be accompanied by an application for a longer period for notification` MEANS
    IF `the accompanying application is personally signed by the Attorney General of the province in which the application for the authorization is made or by the Minister`
       AND `it asks for a period longer than the period mentioned in subsection 196(1)`
       AND `s 185(2) the period does not exceed three years` `the longer period it sets out`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such longer period not exceeding three years as is set out in the application"

-- 185(3): "Where an application for an authorization is accompanied by an application referred to in subsection (2), the judge to whom the applications are made shall first consider the application referred to in subsection (2) and where, on the basis of
-- the affidavit in support of the application for the authorization and any other affidavit evidence submitted in support of the application referred to in subsection (2), the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of
-- the application, he shall fix a period, not exceeding three years, in substitution for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1)." The duty, as decision functions: whether the judge is bound to fix a period, and whether the period fixed is within the limit.
-- src:3860 | Where extension to be granted
-- src:3861 | (3) Where an application for an authorization is accompanied by an application referred to in subsection (2), the judge to whom the applications are made shall first consider the application referred to in subsection (2) and where, on the basis of the affidavit in support of the application for the authorization and any other affidavit evidence submitted in support of the application referred to in subsection (2), the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application, he shall fix a period, not exceeding three years, in substitution for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1).
@ref Criminal Code s 185(3) (src:3860-3861)
GIVEN `the application for an authorization is accompanied by an application referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the basis of the affidavit evidence the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(3) the judge is bound to fix a period in substitution for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application for an authorization is accompanied by an application referred to in subsection (2)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application for an authorization is accompanied by an application referred to in subsection (2)"
        IF `on the basis of the affidavit evidence the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where, on the basis of the affidavit in support of the application for the authorization and any other affidavit evidence submitted in support of the application referred to in subsection (2), the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application"

-- src:3860 | Where extension to be granted
-- src:3861 | (3) Where an application for an authorization is accompanied by an application referred to in subsection (2), the judge to whom the applications are made shall first consider the application referred to in subsection (2) and where, on the basis of the affidavit in support of the application for the authorization and any other affidavit evidence submitted in support of the application referred to in subsection (2), the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant the granting of the application, he shall fix a period, not exceeding three years, in substitution for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1).
@ref Criminal Code s 185(3) (src:3860-3861)
GIVEN `the period the judge fixes` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(3) the period the judge fixes is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `s 185(2) the period does not exceed three years` `the period the judge fixes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he shall fix a period, not exceeding three years"

-- 185(4): "If the judge ... refuses to fix a period in substitution for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1) or if the judge fixes a shorter period than the one set out in the application referred to in subsection (2), the person submitting
-- the application for the authorization may withdraw that application and, if it is withdrawn, the judge shall not proceed to consider it or to give the authorization and shall destroy, or return to that person, both applications and all other material pertaining to them."
-- src:3862 | If extension not granted
-- src:3863 | (4) If the judge to whom an application for an authorization and an application referred to in subsection (2) are made refuses to fix a period in substitution for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1) or if the judge fixes a shorter period than the one set out in the application referred to in subsection (2), the person submitting the application for the authorization may withdraw that application and, if it is withdrawn, the judge shall not proceed to consider it or to give the authorization and shall destroy, or return to that person, both applications and all other material pertaining to them.
@ref Criminal Code s 185(4) (src:3862-3863)
GIVEN `the judge refused to fix a period in substitution for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge fixed a shorter period than the one set out in the application referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(4) the person submitting the application for the authorization may withdraw it` MEANS
    IF `the judge refused to fix a period in substitution for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1)` OR `the judge fixed a shorter period than the one set out in the application referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the judge to whom an application for an authorization and an application referred to in subsection (2) are made refuses to fix a period"

-- src:3862 | If extension not granted
-- src:3863 | (4) If the judge to whom an application for an authorization and an application referred to in subsection (2) are made refuses to fix a period in substitution for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1) or if the judge fixes a shorter period than the one set out in the application referred to in subsection (2), the person submitting the application for the authorization may withdraw that application and, if it is withdrawn, the judge shall not proceed to consider it or to give the authorization and shall destroy, or return to that person, both applications and all other material pertaining to them.
@ref Criminal Code s 185(4) (src:3862-3863)
GIVEN `the application for the authorization has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(4) the judge shall not proceed to consider the application or to give the authorization` MEANS
    IF `the application for the authorization has been withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is withdrawn, the judge shall not proceed to consider it or to give the authorization"

-- src:3862 | If extension not granted
-- src:3863 | (4) If the judge to whom an application for an authorization and an application referred to in subsection (2) are made refuses to fix a period in substitution for the period mentioned in subsection 196(1) or if the judge fixes a shorter period than the one set out in the application referred to in subsection (2), the person submitting the application for the authorization may withdraw that application and, if it is withdrawn, the judge shall not proceed to consider it or to give the authorization and shall destroy, or return to that person, both applications and all other material pertaining to them.
@ref Criminal Code s 185(4) (src:3862-3863)
GIVEN `the application for the authorization has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(4) the judge is bound to destroy, or return to the person who submitted them, both applications and all other material` MEANS
    IF `the application for the authorization has been withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is withdrawn, the judge shall not proceed to consider it or to give the authorization and shall destroy, or return to that person, both applications and all other material pertaining to them"
